<?xml version="1.0"?>
<model>
  <name>Nav UGV</name>
  <version>1.0</version>
  <sdf version="1.6">model.sdf</sdf>

  <author>
    <name>TerraLink nav</name>
    <email>software.guild@smail.iitm.ac.in</email>
  </author>

  <description>
    A small differential-drive ground rover (chassis + 2 driven wheels + a
    passive caster + a planar lidar), self-authored directly in native
    Ignition SDF - not vendored as-is.

    Shape/component list (chassis box, two driven wheels, a caster, a
    forward-facing planar lidar) is adapted from
    src/d3/my_bot/description/robot_core.xacro + lidar.xacro, per this
    project's plan to reuse d3's proven UGV rather than design a new one.
    It's expressed as plain SDF here (not URDF/xacro + robot_state_publisher)
    for the same reason `models/iris_quad` is plain SDF rather than a
    PX4-style xacro: this project's simulation stack (Ignition Gazebo
    Fortress) spawns and controls robots natively via SDF include blocks +
    Ignition system plugins, and every other model in this project already
    follows that convention.

    d3's actuation plugin (Gazebo CLASSIC's libgazebo_ros_diff_drive.so) and
    sensor plugin (libgazebo_ros_ray_sensor.so) are NOT usable under
    Ignition Fortress - both are replaced here with Ignition's own native
    equivalents (the DiffDrive system plugin, attached at include time in
    worlds/room_maze.world, matching iris_quad's own pattern of attaching
    control plugins at include time rather than baking them into the model;
    and a native `gpu_lidar` sensor, which - like iris_quad's rgbd_camera -
    needs no separate plugin block at all, since the world's already-loaded
    Sensors system plugin picks up every sensor type automatically).

    A later, step05 addition: a front-facing, downward-tilted `rgbd_camera`
    (see model.sdf's own comment on `front_camera_link`) - lets the UGV
    itself observe terrain (e.g. inside a tunnel/culvert) that `emap`'s
    overhead UAV camera can never see, feeding the same shared
    /elevation_map. See docs/work-docs/nav/step05_frontier_tunnel_navigation.md.
  </description>
</model>
